title: Walking with God – The Old Man and the New
description: The Christian walk, part one: walking with God daily in prayer and the word, putting off the old man and putting on the new, how sin gets back in, and counting the cost of discipleship, from the teachings on the walk.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-walk-with-god.html

# The first of five decks on studies/data/topics/walk.json (the user's call): this one covers the themes
# "Walking with God", "The old man and the new" and "The cost of discipleship", each given the same weight.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.

=== Introduction
--- Walking with God [title]
overline: Doctrine · The walk
heading: Walking with God
sub: Separation, service, and walking with God. Part one: the daily walk, the old man and the new, and the cost of discipleship.
refs: Genesis 5:24; Galatians 5:16; Luke 9:23; Romans 12:1-2
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 6558
--- Enoch walked with God
big: Genesis 5:24 | mark: Enoch walked with God
p: When we look at these early patriarchs, we can see the pattern for salvation. Adam knows God, his creator, and knows his sin. Abel brings the blood of atonement, given in faith. Seth and Enos, that with the mouth, confession is made, calling upon the name of the Lord. And with Enoch, we have the testimony that he walked with God, that he lived separated, pleasing God.
big: Hebrews 11:5 | mark: he had this testimony, that he pleased God

# from 10828
--- A daily choice
lead: The fruits of the Spirit don't come automatically. Just because we are saved doesn't mean that we will do good. Just as it doesn't mean we will stop sinning.
big: Luke 9:23 | mark: take up his cross daily, and follow me
p: It's a daily choice. It is on us to reject the temptations of the flesh by walking in the spirit.

=== Walking with God daily
# from 9102, 13308
--- Our daily bread
kicker: Walking with God daily
lead: It is our daily walk with God that protects us. We ask Him to provide our daily bread, not just physical need for food, but spiritually, studying the word of God.
p: We start our day in prayer, talking to God, and reading His word that His will be made known to us. His promises made clear that we may grow in faith. This is how we resist temptation.
big: Joshua 1:8 | mark: thou shalt meditate therein day and night

# from 7745, 8711
--- How to increase your faith
kicker: Walking with God daily
lead: How to increase your faith? The Bible tells us:
xr: Romans 10:17 | Read the word and listen to preaching from His word
xr: James 1:22 | By living the word we begin to rely more on God and less on ourselves
xr: Psalm 51:12 | Pray for faith
xr: Malachi 3:10 | Obey His word and see how His blessings reward your faith
p: If you are feeling rudderless. If you are searching for more faith. If you don't know what you should do. Start with the word.

# from 10503, 17585
--- Beginning each day with Him
kicker: Walking with God daily
p: The first fruits are His. The first sons of Israel. The first of the flock. The first tenth of your earnings. All His. And as we begin each day as His, seeking first the kingdom of God.
p: A believer makes the conscious decision to make Jesus their companion. To wake early in the morning, starting the day with Christ, and His word. In prayer.
refs: Matthew 6:33; 1 Corinthians 15:31; Song of Solomon 7:10-12

# from 17577
--- The bride who would not open
kicker: Walking with God daily
scripture: Song of Solomon 5:2-3 | mark: Open to me; I have put off my coat; how shall I put it on
p: She makes excuses. Rather than hear His voice and do His will, a believer may see their contentment and undefiled spirit as a bed to rest upon. When God asks so little of us whom He has saved, to open when He knocks, will we respond?
big: Revelation 3:20 | mark: Behold, I stand at the door, and knock

# from 12109, 17412, 14633
--- In good times and bad
kicker: Walking with God daily
lead: It is vitally important for a Christian to not wait until there's trouble in their life to take their walk seriously. To turn to the Lord in praise and thanksgiving when times are good.
big: Proverbs 30:8-9 | mark: give me neither poverty nor riches
p: Like Paul we need to work on being content ([[Philippians 4:11-12]]). We are better to stoke our zeal for the Lord as a fire, and keep it going as warm embers for our entire life, than burn out quickly and fade like Jehu ([[2 Kings 10:16]] · [[2 Kings 10:31]]).
