read: app:doctrine-walk~7745 | How to increase your faith
read: app:doctrine-walk~17577 | The bride who would not open
read: app:doctrine-walk~17412 | Give me neither poverty nor riches

=== The old man and the new
# from 4662, 4915
--- Put off the old man
kicker: The old man and the new
scripture: Ephesians 4:22-24 | mark: put off; the old man; put on the new man
p: In grace, through Jesus, we have a new man, created by the Spirit, and that Spirit convicts us in our sin. Where the reprobate is past feeling, we are made all the more sensitive to God's will.
p: If we be saved, children of light, then seek the things of Heaven ([[Colossians 3:1-2]]). Putting off anger, wrath, malice, blasphemy, filthy communication, the behavior of the unsaved that acts as a bushel to hide our light.

# from 10802, 10822, 10823
--- The spirit willing, the flesh weak
kicker: The old man and the new
big: Romans 6:1-2 | mark: Shall we continue in sin, that grace may abound? God forbid
p: Paul is really hammering this point home because it is not automatic that we who are saved turn from our sins. Our new man, inside, quickened by the Holy Ghost, sealed unto the day of redemption, knows not sin. But the old man still reigns in our members. Our flesh.
big: Romans 7:18-19 | mark: for to will is present with me; but how to perform that which is good I find not
p: We sin, every day. But unlike the unsaved, which we were and should never forget, we have the Spirit within us, and our own spiritual new man cries out to do good.

# from 10824
--- Sanctification is not about salvation
kicker: The old man and the new
lead: Our sanctification isn't about salvation. It is about becoming acceptable tools in God's shed. To be workmen who aren't ashamed. Good and faithful servants.
p: If we walk in the spirit we will also learn more about the holiness of God and His law, and in that knowledge come to see more things that are sinful. It is a refining process. One that removes thorns in our flesh we didn't know we had.
p: It's not about you. We are saved already, and justified by the perfect work of Christ Jesus that we believe on. Rejoice.

# from 9100, 9101, 3825
--- It is written
kicker: The old man and the new
lead: It wasn't His divine nature that saved His human flesh from falling, but His doing His Father's will, and clinging to the word.
xr: Luke 4:4 | Bread: *Man shall not live by bread alone, but by every word of God*
xr: Luke 4:8 | Power: *Thou shalt worship the Lord thy God, and him only shalt thou serve*
xr: Luke 4:12 | Presumption: *Thou shalt not tempt the Lord thy God*
big: 1 Corinthians 10:13 | mark: will with the temptation also make a way to escape
p: That way of escape is found in our knowledge of the word. By how much time we spend in it.

# from 4722
--- The whole armour of God
kicker: The old man and the new
scripture: Ephesians 6:13-17 | mark: the whole armour of God; the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God
p: We are equipped with these things, when we walk in them. And if we walk in them, we should have no fear of the wicked. *If God be for us, who can be against us?* ([[Romans 8:31]])
read: app:doctrine-walk~4662 | Put off the old man, put on the new
read: app:doctrine-walk~10822 | The spirit willing but the flesh weak
read: app:doctrine-walk~10824 | Our sanctification is not about salvation
