=== How sin gets back in
# from 14235
--- How sin compounds
kicker: How sin gets back in
lead: David tarried in bed, rather than in battle. And rather than refresh himself in the Spirit, thinking of the things of the Lord, he wandered.
p: When we do that, blow off our commitments, “take a day off” from prayer or study, we often wander, too. David goes from a momentary lapse in duty and honor to premeditated murder. This is how Christians backslide. This is how sin compounds.
big: 2 Samuel 11:1-2 | mark: But David tarried still at Jerusalem

# from 13355, 14094, 13990
--- After a victory
kicker: How sin gets back in
lead: The devil loves to bring a test before us when God is in the process of rewarding our faith in Him. When we are the most comfortable.
p: Many times in the Christian life, you will find that you've made it through something by walking in the Spirit and trusting in God, only to stumble at the finish line because the relief turns to complacency. Beware of the sin of Achan ([[Joshua 7:21]]). A battle isn't the war.
big: 1 Peter 5:8 | mark: Be sober, be vigilant

# from 14705, 15208, 15336
--- Blessing should humble us
kicker: How sin gets back in
lead: A great triumph of the Lord acting miraculously in our lives, followed by a low point where we forget the trouble we were in, and grow comfortable, taking it for granted.
p: Hezekiah, recovered from his deathbed, showed the envoys of Babylon all his treasures rather than praising the Lord ([[2 Kings 20:13]]). Uzziah allowed pride in himself for the victories and blessings given of God to put himself where he ought not be ([[2 Chronicles 26:16]]).
take: When we are blessed by the Lord, it should humble us. Stay humble.

# from 7191, 12520, 10080
--- Pottage and quail
kicker: How sin gets back in
panel: Esau's pottage | Christians who live carnally, despising their birthright received through Christ, losing blessings of God for a simple bowl of pottage, are like Esau. How many times do we do the same, for much less? [[Hebrews 12:16-17]]
panel: Quail at the nostrils | If you stumble back into sin, you find it doesn't hold the same appeal. In short order you'll see it as repulsive. You will have it coming out of your nostrils. [[Numbers 11:20]]
p: We forget where we were. We forget how we escaped. We melt down the treasure God provided, and *the people sat down to eat and drink, and rose up to play* ([[1 Corinthians 10:7]]).

# from 14236, 16449
--- The Father's rod, and restoration
kicker: How sin gets back in
big: Hebrews 12:6 | mark: For whom the Lord loveth he chasteneth
p: Especially knowing that, as adopted children, our Father will not spare the rod, and the sins we do in secret will be revealed in the light.
p: And even if we have made mistakes in our past, there's still reconciliation with God because we are saved. If we turn from our wicked ways, and walk in His paths, we can be restored and do great works for the Lord.
refs: Proverbs 28:13; 1 John 1:9
