read: app:doctrine-walk~13355 | Beware the sin of Achan
read: app:doctrine-walk~15841 | Spiritual triumph wounded by pride
read: app:doctrine-walk~7191 | Esau sold his birthright for pottage

=== The cost of discipleship
# from 9487, 9490
--- Discipleship, not salvation
kicker: The cost of discipleship
scripture: Luke 14:26-27 | mark: whosoever doth not bear his cross, and come after me, cannot be my disciple
p: Many mistakenly think this passage is about salvation, not discipleship. Some believe that He is describing a works-based salvation. But even more common is to think that by belief unto redemption they have picked up that cross. That discipleship comes naturally with being born again.
p: Jesus doesn't mean that we should hate them, or ourselves, but that we be willing to give them up, and more, our very lives, because we love Him all the more.

# from 9488
--- Count the cost
kicker: The cost of discipleship
scripture: Luke 14:28-34 | mark: counteth the cost; if the salt have lost his savour
p: Jesus wasn't trying to discourage us from being His disciples, but dividing the chaff from the wheat, being honest with those of us who remain. Every born again believer is called to be in service to Christ. It is time to consider the cost.

# from 9524, 9523
--- Willing to die, but not to be inconvenienced
kicker: The cost of discipleship
lead: Most saved Christians will tell you that they would gladly lay down their life for the cause of Christ.
p: But how many saved Christians are willing to lay down 15-20 minutes of our morning to read the Bible? To go to church once a week, let alone three times a week? To go door knocking and soul winning? How can we expect to seriously be willing to go to our death for professing the name of Christ if we won't be inconvenienced a little bit here and there?
big: Luke 16:13 | mark: Ye cannot serve God and mammon

# from 5145, 9947
--- Not peace, but a sword
kicker: The cost of discipleship
big: Matthew 10:34-37 | mark: I came not to send peace, but a sword
p: If you have been born again for any length of time, you have experienced this. Especially within family. Those that know us best and who refuse the truth, resent and turn on us.
p: The final excuse many of us have against doing God's will for us is the anger and confrontation we will have with loved ones. As Moses with Zipporah at the inn ([[Exodus 4:24-26]]).

# from 5944, 4089
--- A good soldier of Jesus Christ
kicker: The cost of discipleship
big: 2 Timothy 2:3-4 | mark: endure hardness, as a good soldier of Jesus Christ
p: To endure hardness like a soldier. Not entangled with any other cause or cares, but the one he's been drafted to.
p: Gideon's 300 placing lamps in earthen vessels, that are then broken to reveal the light ([[Judges 7:16]]). This is such an amazing parallel to our lives.

--- A good soldier of Jesus Christ, continued
kicker: The cost of discipleship
big: 2 Corinthians 4:7 | mark: we have this treasure in earthen vessels
